---
import Guide from '../../layouts/Guide.astro';
const faqs = [
  { question: 'How many digits is a US ZIP code?', answer: 'Five. The extended ZIP+4 format has nine digits written as 12345-6789.' },
  { question: 'Can a ZIP code start with 0?', answer: 'Yes. ZIP codes in New England, New Jersey and Puerto Rico start with 0 (for example 02108 in Boston). Store ZIP codes as text, not numbers, so spreadsheets keep the leading zero.' },
  { question: 'What is the lowest ZIP code?', answer: '00501, a unique ZIP code for the IRS in Holtsville, New York. The lowest residential ZIP codes are in Puerto Rico, starting at 00601.' },
];
const regions = [
  ['0', 'Northeast', 'CT, MA, ME, NH, NJ, PR, RI, VT, VI, military (AE)'],
  ['1', 'Northeast', 'DE, NY, PA'],
  ['2', 'Mid-Atlantic', 'DC, MD, NC, SC, VA, WV'],
  ['3', 'Southeast', 'AL, FL, GA, MS, TN, military (AA)'],
  ['4', 'Great Lakes', 'IN, KY, MI, OH'],
  ['5', 'Upper Midwest', 'IA, MN, MT, ND, SD, WI'],
  ['6', 'Central', 'IL, KS, MO, NE'],
  ['7', 'South Central', 'AR, LA, OK, TX'],
  ['8', 'Mountain', 'AZ, CO, ID, NM, NV, UT, WY'],
  ['9', 'Pacific', 'AK, CA, HI, OR, WA, GU, AS, MP, military (AP)'],
];
---

<Guide slug="us-zip-code-format" description="US ZIP codes have 5 digits: a national area, a sectional center, and a post office. See the region map behind the first digit and how ZIP+4 works." faqs={faqs}>
  <h1>US ZIP code format, digit by digit</h1>
  <p class="lead" data-answer>A US ZIP code has <strong>five digits</strong>. The first digit is a national area, the next two identify a regional mail-processing center, and the last two point to a specific post office or delivery zone. An optional four-digit <a href="/guides/what-is-zip-plus-4/">ZIP+4</a> can follow after a hyphen.</p>

  <div class="not-prose my-8 rounded-xl border border-line bg-surface p-6">
    <div class="flex justify-center gap-2 font-mono text-4xl font-semibold sm:text-5xl">
      <span class="rounded-lg bg-stamp-soft px-3 py-2 text-stamp">9</span>
      <span class="rounded-lg bg-brand-soft px-3 py-2 text-brand">0</span>
      <span class="rounded-lg bg-brand-soft px-3 py-2 text-brand">2</span>
      <span class="rounded-lg bg-manila px-3 py-2 text-ink">1</span>
      <span class="rounded-lg bg-manila px-3 py-2 text-ink">0</span>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 grid grid-cols-3 text-center text-sm text-ink-3">
      <span>National area</span><span>Sectional center</span><span>Post office</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>The first digit: national areas</h2>
  <p>ZIP codes start at 0 in the Northeast and increase heading west:</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Digit</th><th>Area</th><th>States &amp; territories</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>{regions.map(([d, a, s]) => <tr><td><strong>{d}</strong></td><td>{a}</td><td>{s}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Digits two and three: the sectional center</h2>
  <p>The first three digits together form a <strong>ZIP3</strong> prefix that identifies a sectional center facility (SCF) — the processing plant that sorts mail for a region. All ZIP codes that begin with 100–102, for example, are in Manhattan.</p>

  <h2>Digits four and five: the post office</h2>
  <p>The final two digits narrow mail down to a single post office, station or delivery area. Low numbers often (but not always) belong to the main post office in the SCF’s city.</p>

  <h2>ZIP+4</h2>
  <p>Adding a hyphen and four more digits — <code>90210-1234</code> — identifies a block face, a floor of a building, or a group of PO boxes. It is optional for everyday mail. Read <a href="/guides/what-is-zip-plus-4/">What is ZIP+4?</a> for details.</p>

  <h2>Formatting tips</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Write the ZIP code on the same line as the city and state: <code>BOSTON MA 02108</code>.</li>
    <li>Keep leading zeros. In spreadsheets, format ZIP columns as text.</li>
    <li>Validate that a code has exactly five digits (optionally followed by <code>-</code> and four digits).</li>
  </ul>
</Guide>
